Day 22: The Law of Love | Wednesday of the Third Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
At the center of everything —
beneath every commandment,
beneath every teaching,
beneath every spiritual practice —
is love.

Welcome to Day 22 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection brings us back to the heart of holiness:
not rules,
not rituals,
not complexity —
but love lived out in daily life.

Jesus answers the greatest question with the greatest clarity:
“Love God with all your heart… and love your neighbor as yourself.”  
This spoken‑word devotional invites you to let that love shape your day —
in patience,
in compassion,
in forgiveness,
in the quiet, hidden choices only God sees.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why holiness is simply love made visible

How loving God means letting Him into every part of your life

How loving your neighbor becomes real in small, everyday moments

A prayer to grow in love

A simple daily activity: one quiet act of kindness

If this reflection blesses you, consider continuing the journey through all 40 days of Lent.

Peace be with you.

